        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 2 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "No ordering signal (no data dependency, `source()` call, or numeric filename prefix) distinguishes the run order of these files. They may need to run in a specific order that could not be determined automatically — check this before running.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:2, File = c(\"lib_setup.R\", \"lib_user.R\"\n), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"—\"), Basis = c(\"none\", \"none\")), row.names = c(NA, \n-2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 2 scripts: 2 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions. \n\n*a script hit a `could not find function \"...\"` error; we added the `library()` calls it needs (see below), and re-ran once. The outcomes above are from that corrected run.*",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"lib_setup.R\", \"lib_user.R\"), Outcome = c(\"ran_ok\", \n\"ran_ok\"), Detail = c(\"\", \"\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, \n-2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "**`library()` calls added**",
          "**1 script uses functions from packages it does not load itself.** The packages are usually loaded in another script of the project, which only helps when the scripts run in one R session in the right order. To run it we added the `library()` calls below at the top. Any such script that then ran is **reproducible only after adding `library()` calls it should make itself**.",
          "Reproducible after adding `library()` calls: lib_user.R.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"lib_user.R\", \"library() calls added\" = \"library(tools)\"), row.names = \"lib_user.R\", class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — lib_setup.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> library(tools)\n> x <- file_path_sans_ext(\"data.csv\")\n> cat(x, \"\\n\")\ndata \n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — lib_user.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> library(tools)\n> y <- file_ext(\"data.csv\")\n> cat(y, \"\\n\")\ncsv \n````\n\n:::\n"
